# Local data. The archive is rebuildable from upstream git history, so it is
# never committed - and the duckdb file is far too large for a repo.
#
# EXCEPT data/build/manifest.yaml. It is the ONLY hand-maintained input to the
# build monitor -- source, not derived data -- and docs/HANDOFF_CLAUDE_CODE.md
# requires it to change in the same commit as docs/PLAN.md. That is impossible
# while it is ignored, and losing data/ would lose it. git cannot re-include a
# file whose parent directory is excluded, hence the per-level re-inclusion.
data/*
!data/build/
data/build/*
!data/build/manifest.yaml
#
# And data/review/ -- the charter, the sealed cycles and the append-only inbox
# are the record of how this build was steered, not derived output. The inbox is
# append-only, so a concurrent-append merge conflict is ALWAYS resolved by
# keeping BOTH sides in timestamp order. Never resolve one by dropping a line.
# data/results/review_state.json* stays ignored -- that one IS derived.
!data/review/
!data/review/**
#
# And data/fleet/ -- node cards and heartbeats. Same reason as data/review/:
# not derived output, but the evidence that a node exists and is alive. Without
# this re-inclusion `git add data/fleet` silently adds nothing, so a node
# registers locally, looks joined, and stays invisible to every other machine --
# a declaration standing in for evidence, which is the failure this fleet design
# exists to prevent. Found on ZoltarOne's first join, 2026-09-04.
!data/fleet/
!data/fleet/**
# Secrets. .env.example IS tracked; .env never is.
.env
.env.local

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
/build/
/dist/
